TzD (task #52): procps_scan clears the tail of procps_status_t from sp.
memset(&sp->vsz, 0, sizeof(*sp) - offsetof(procps_status_t, vsz)) clears
from the vsz member to the end of the struct through a pointer to that
one member, which TzD bounds to the member (the write traps in ps).
Address the tail from the struct with offsetof: the same bytes, bounded
by the struct.
--- a/libbb/procps.c	2026-11-14 01:26:52.654137983 +0900
+++ b/libbb/procps.c	2026-11-14 01:26:52.671691427 +0900
@@ -329,7 +329,8 @@
 		 * "continue": try next /proc/XXX
 		 */
 
-		memset(&sp->vsz, 0, sizeof(*sp) - offsetof(procps_status_t, vsz));
+		memset((char *)sp + offsetof(procps_status_t, vsz), 0,
+		       sizeof(*sp) - offsetof(procps_status_t, vsz));
 
 		sp->pid = pid;
 		if (!(flags & ~PSSCAN_PID))
